It's been a little while since we had a discussion about lojban  
sounds, so I assume there are probably some new learners around.  
Which means that they might not know about the reader I started  
writing last year. (Although it got about 40 page views in November,  
so some folks know it's there.)

The website is http://www-personal.umich.edu/~alexjm/ and it contains  
both a recording and text of the same content, following the concepts  
taught in Lojban for Beginners though chapter 4.

Just thought that listening to a longer selection of Lojban might  
help somebody out with listening. If you want a really long one, look  
at the "really long MP3" on the main page -- that's about 15 minutes  
of me pronouncing all the CV CVV and CV'V syllables in Lojban.

ki'e mu'o mi'e .aleks.


